# Break-glass restore for app/.htaccess.
#
# This lives outside app/ on purpose. The Access tab in app/admin.php rewrites
# app/.htaccess, and a bad rule there 500s the whole /app/ directory — including
# the admin portal that would undo it. This directory is the way back without
# reaching for SSH.
#
# It also carries its own .htaccess rather than adding a <Files> block to the
# document root's: a mistake in this file breaks only /recover/, whereas a
# mistake in the root one would take down the public landing page with it.
#
# `Require user` rather than the `Require ldap-filter` app/ uses, deliberately.
# It is a plain string comparison against REMOTE_USER handled by mod_authz_user,
# with no LDAP query and no filter syntax to get subtly wrong — and note that
# mod_authnz_ldap wraps a ldap-filter value in its own parentheses, so the
# natural-looking `(uid=aperkel)` would become a doubled ((uid=aperkel)) and
# fail. A recovery path should have the fewest moving parts of anything here.
DirectoryIndex index.php
AuthType CAS
Require user aperkel
